    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5002A\n\nSPONSOR: HELMING\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nfor Ontario county to impose additional rates of sales and compensating\nuse taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to extending the authorization for Ontario County to impose\nadditional rates of sales and compensating use taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Clause 40 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph of\nsection 1210 of the tax law, as amended by section 1 of item FF of\nsubpart C of part XXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020, is amended\n\nSection 2: Provides for an immediate effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Ontario County Board of Supervisors has requested legislation to be\nintroduced in the State Legislature to grant Ontario County the ability\nto extend the additional one-eighth and three-eighths of one percent\nsales and compensating use tax through November 30, 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
